INSTALLATION

This program requires access to a full license for IDL 8 or later, and
to some packages.  Version 8 or later is required because the code
uses the IDL implementation of lists.  Known dependencies include the
IDL Astro library, LAPACK routines (which are part of the standard
distribution), and the CGCOLOR routine, part of David Fanning's IDL
tools.  The CGCOLOR routine is only required if plots are requested.
This version is known to work under Mac OSX (multiple versions)
and is likely to work under other flavors of UNIX.  It is not expected
to work under Windows; the author does not have access to IDL
in a Windows-based system.

The default installation would save all the code in a subdirectory
named IDLCODE, and all the data in a subdirectory named DATA.
Code and data can also be placed in the same directory if desired.
The results of runs (e.g., using the VARS procedure)
can be placed in diffeent directories if desired; since VARS
produces many output files, using a different directory is recommended.

The main routine org_v3p9 is designed primarily for use from the IDL
command line.  The author does not use the IDL Development Environment
or workbench, so he cannot provide advice on how to use the routines
in that environment, but all commands used are close to IDL standard,
so it is expected that any required changes will be minor.

